Q55. Explain Difference between Serialization and Deserialization and also transient ?
Serialization :
 - Definition → The process of converting an object into a byte stream so it can be saved to a file, database, or sent over a network.
 - Why? → Java objects live in memory (RAM). Serialization allows persisting or transferring them.
 - How?
    a. A class must implement Serializable marker interface.
    b. Use ObjectOutputStream to write the object.
Deserialization :
    - Definition → The process of converting a byte stream back into an object.
    - How?
       a. Use ObjectInputStream to read the object.
transient Keyword :
     - Definition → Used to skip a field during serialization. That field will not be saved in the byte stream.
     - Why? → To protect sensitive data (like passwords, security keys, bank details) or non-serializable objects.

