        a. Java keeps all string literals in a shared memory area called String Pool.
        b. If strings were changeable, changing one string would affect all references pointing to it.
        c. Immutable strings make reusing memory safe and fast.
 - Thread-Safety:
         a. Immutable strings are safe to use in multiple threads because their value never changes.
         b. No need for extra locks or synchronization.

